  "estimatedMinutes": 20,
  "instructions": "## Four departments, one block\n\nA polytechnic has the block `192.168.10.0/24` and four departments of about 50 machines each: Admin, Science, Arts and the Library. One router, R1, has an interface for each department. The router interfaces are already addressed with the **first usable address** of each subnet.\n\n## Do this\n\n1. Work out the mask that splits the /24 into four equal subnets, and the four network addresses. The **Subnet calculator** tab can check your working. Type the answers on the right.\n2. Click each PC and give it an address in its own department's subnet, with the right mask and the router interface as gateway. Read the router's interface addresses to see which subnet each department is in.\n3. Ping from Admin to the Library PC, then press **Check my network**.",
